# PN-Ultra-Audit: findings checked by hand and accepted. Each line names the file and the rules;
# everything else in these files is still audited, and suppressed findings are counted in the report.
#
# The redaction module's documentation and tests must contain fake secrets to prove they are hidden:
# the AWS key there is the example published in AWS's own documentation, and the rest is in `#[cfg(test)]`.
crates/engine/src/guard/secrets.rs     SEC-*
# A Cargo workspace has one lockfile, at the root (Cargo.lock), shared by every member crate.
crates/*/Cargo.toml                    DEP-NO-LOCKFILE
xtask/Cargo.toml                       DEP-NO-LOCKFILE
# The brain view draws a graph; it holds no wallet or key, and Math.random only paces animation.
crates/report/src/brain/brain.js       WEB3-*
# Fixtures for the documentation ratchet; `fit` there is a Rust function, not Jasmine's focused test.
xtask/tests/fixtures/*                 TST-FOCUSED
# Rust tests live in `#[cfg(test)]` modules beside the code and in each crate's tests/ folder
# (1,390 of them), which this per-file heuristic does not match.
crates                                 TST-MODULE-UNTESTED
# docs/architecture.md and docs/adr/ exist; the rule does not see them.
*                                      DOC-NO-ARCH
# The release notes show the documented install command; install.sh verifies the SHA-256 it downloads.
.github/workflows/release.yml          SH-CURL-PIPE
